[{:db/id 17592186119833 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2a383fb4-f81d-5536-bfab-907adbefb459"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2a383fb4-f81d-5536-bfab-907adbefb459" :question/id #uuid "2a383fb4-f81d-5536-bfab-907adbefb459" :question/math-academy-id "q-128372" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(7,4,-3)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-2}{4}=\\frac{z+1}{-2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨7,4,-3⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨5,4,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨5,4,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =⟨7,4,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =57\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =57 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z & =57 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z-57 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ab781c91-252d-5387-b0ba-ee29d18b5ea0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ab781c91-252d-5387-b0ba-ee29d18b5ea0" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab781c91-252d-5387-b0ba-ee29d18b5ea0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dd9f7bca-6210-53d4-939e-d73b38d6642a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-37e5c1f6-5233-50a9-a0c7-3d8454d96058" "answer-b722b988-b76f-5900-8ce4-497e838c929c" "answer-8a9aa20e-7044-5fe9-999a-ca209eb00faf" "answer-dd9f7bca-6210-53d4-939e-d73b38d6642a" "answer-44b25bde-c138-5e61-9bfe-10c541da03de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37e5c1f6-5233-50a9-a0c7-3d8454d96058" :answer/id #uuid "37e5c1f6-5233-50a9-a0c7-3d84